      "confidence": 0.85,
      "curator_note": "Alpha cleavage on the acetyl side: loss of the methyl radical (.CH3, C7) with formation of the C5#O6+ acylium, giving the C5H9O+ pentanoyl/valeroyl cation C4H9-C#O+ (m/z 85, 2%). Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.2 is a thermochemical fragmentation map (log k printed above each reaction arrow, heats of formation printed below each species), not a curved-arrow figure. All electron moves here are curator-inferred from the mechanism-type label printed under the reaction arrow; none is drawn on the page. Canonical THREE fishhooks: move<1> O6 odd electron into the forming C5-O6 pi bond, move<2> one C5-C7 electron into that pi bond, move<3> the other C5-C7 electron onto C7 (departing methyl radical)."
    },
