      "curator_note": "Cross-linked to IMS_8_2_alpha_0_7. MISMATCH (bond order): the rule cleaves the correct bond (their C14-C15 = my C5-C7, expelling [C.]15 = my methyl radical) but its product acylium is written '[C]14[O+]19' with a SINGLE C-O bond, leaving C14 divalent -- it never upgrades the carbonyl to the C#O+ triple bond that an acylium requires. This record encodes the chemically correct C5#O6+ acylium; the MØD rule is under-bonded. Listed in rule_mismatches."
